            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. The protein in bone broth powder is mostly collagen, which contains no tryptophan and is low in leucine and several other essential amino acids. That gives it a protein quality score of zero on the PDCAAS scale. The grams are real, but they should supplement complete proteins like meat, eggs, dairy or a good plant blend rather than replace them."
